# f1 = fill, f2 = called, f3 = the function stored under add
# The universal form of a library: the names are stored and the marker is laid by a descriptor. The definition leaves the LAYOUT the change GetsAccessor: the run time's leave for a redefinition: it stays.
# But every definition on this record is in sight and under a WRITTEN key, and none is under `add`: that FIELD is never redefined (FieldStability::IsNeverRedefined: the run time ends the process where one is, field by field).
# So its empty slot says that the name is missing: the read needs no look at the cell, its type is the cell's, the call of what is no function throws and meets nothing: no closed arm stands in the loop.
# RUN(LAYOUT): link layouts mechanisms=all
# LAYOUT: layout L0 changes=[IsFrozen, GainsProperty, GetsAccessor]
# RUN(FIELD): link fields mechanisms=all
# FIELD: "add" appended proven={{*}}f3 {{*}}beside-what-descriptors-define
# RUN(MARKER): link fields mechanisms=all
# MARKER-NOT: "marker" {{*}}beside-what-descriptors-define
# RUN(CALLED): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CALLED: = GetSlotOrUndefined {{*}}key="add" receivers=[L0] level=Proven
# RUN(LOOK): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# LOOK-NOT: = HasNoFieldOutsideSlot
